# Quantity models and their Law schemes

Chapter 5, §§5.1–5.3. Fixed domains carry quantity assignments into any
coefficient algebra. Their written Laws give universal residuals in a
polynomial algebra. The residual quotient represents Law models and
identifies the unique closed factorization of a lawful point. The
examples compute the algebra, module, inverse and infinitesimal cases.
